# 
# https://w3id.org/lcanet/activity#Technosphere
<https://w3id.org/lcanet/activity#Technosphere> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/lcanet/activity#Technosphere> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/lcanet/activity#EnvironemntalType> .
<https://w3id.org/lcanet/activity#Technosphere> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Represents the system of human activities and industrial processes \nwithin the life cycle of a product or service. It encompasses all transformations \nand exchanges of intermediate flows occurring within the economic system." .
<https://w3id.org/lcanet/activity#Technosphere> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Technosphere" .
# 
# https://w3id.org/lcanet/activity#WasteFlow
<https://w3id.org/lcanet/activity#WasteFlow> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/lcanet/activity#WasteFlow> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/lcanet/activity#IntermediateFlow> .
<https://w3id.org/lcanet/activity#WasteFlow> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Represents an intermediate flow within the technosphere corresponding to materials or substances that are discarded by an activity and require further treatment, recovery, or disposal. \nThese flows are typically characterized by the absence of positive economic value for the producing activity." .
<https://w3id.org/lcanet/activity#WasteFlow> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Waste Flow" .
